# Benewake TFMini Plus lidar as the altitude source, Pixhawk 2.4.8 single fan thrust vectoring vehicle.
# Load this AFTER edf_tvc_pixhawk.param, AFTER the board has rebooted, and AFTER the ground station has re-read the parameters from
# the board (Mission Planner: Refresh Params, or disconnect and reconnect). RNGFND1_MIN, MAX, GNDCLR, ORIENT and POS_X/Y/Z do not
# exist on the board while RNGFND1_TYPE is 0, and a ground station holding the old list reports them as missing
# ("No matching Params").
#
# Wiring: sensor +5V, GND, TXD to the board RX and RXD to the board TX of the SERIAL 4/5 port, the #4 pins (section 5.5a of
# DEPLOY_AND_WIRING.md). Wire colours differ between units: read the datasheet of yours.
# Check the lidar before loading this file: Mission Planner, Flight Data, Status tab, "rangefinder1" must show a distance.

# The sensor looks straight down (25 = pitch 270). The TFMini Plus reads 0.1 m to 12 m. 6 is the outdoor value from the
# ArduPilot documentation. Use 10 indoors. Do not set it above what the sensor reads reliably in your light.
RNGFND1_ORIENT    25
RNGFND1_MIN       0.1
RNGFND1_MAX       6

# MEASURE THIS. The distance from the sensor to the ground with the vehicle on its legs, in metres (0.05 to 1.5). It must be
# at least RNGFND1_MIN. The EKF height is the lidar distance minus this value, so a wrong value is a height error on the ground
# and in the air: 0.20 here is a placeholder, not a measurement.
RNGFND1_GNDCLR    0.20

# Sensor position from the centre of the vehicle (the IMU), in metres, forward / right / down. Measure it. It corrects the
# reading for the lever arm when the vehicle tilts. Zero is acceptable at 0.5 m if the sensor is close to the centre line.
# RNGFND1_POS_X   0
# RNGFND1_POS_Y   0
# RNGFND1_POS_Z   0

# Height from the lidar (2 = rangefinder). Keep this LAST: until it is loaded the height comes from the barometer.
# THE LIDAR IS THEN THE ONLY HEIGHT SOURCE. The EKF only has height while it reads between RNGFND1_MIN and RNGFND1_MAX over flat,
# matt ground. If it fails the vehicle has no height: land at once.
# Note: a target of 0.5 m is a LIDAR READING of 0.5 m. It does not subtract RNGFND1_GNDCLR, so the feet are 0.5 - GNDCLR above the ground.
EK3_SRC1_POSZ     2
